  Yesterday I had my next, a bit unusual win. A lvl 21 Samurai ascended with
~1400000 points. Unusual was, that I prayed only once in the entire game
(somewhere in the beginning when in trouble with orcs). I wanted to pray
only in real need, and the real need never came... Similarly, the E-word
was never in use.
  Also, I used only 4 wishes (kept the WoW with one charge 'for later' 
and lost it finally - my mother always told me not to put unidentified wands
into the bag of holding ;-) No luck with other means of getting wishes -
and I have found 5 thrones (sigh).
  I also found two amulets of life saving - and escaped with both of them...
In fact I very seldom went below half of my HP (147 at the end) - seems that
either the character was overdeveloped, or nethack is too easy at late stages.
When escaping I knew 12 spells - but only 3 of them ever used (magic missile
and force bolt when I wanted to keep some monsters at a distance, and
one use of knock on the castle door).

  To the discussion about most useful item - I relied mostly (apart from my
+7 Excalibur - the only weapon I used) on the helm of telepathy. Especially
in hell it is very helpful to know what to expect behind the next corner
without the need to walk blinded.

  So, it seems I now need a more challenging game. My ideas:
- less 'permanent' intrinsics. I made myself fast and invisible with a help
  of wands - I think the wand effects should wear off after some time.
- Limit usage of 'permanent' magic items - things like helm of telepathy
  or gauntlets of power should either get used up after some time or draw
  powers (HP, energy points?) from the character - similarly to the rings
  which draw more food when in use.
- The high level characters heal a fair bit to fast - what does it mean, that
  after an encounter with a black dragon I am fully healed in 10 steps (no
  magic involved)?
- In the very beginning too much depends on luck in finding certain objects.
  I think nethack should be reworked a bit to ensure that in the first
  (say) four levels you can find a reasonably sized general store and an 
  altar. To avoid making it too easy - forbid very powerful items (artifacts,
  certain wands, scroll of genocide etc) from this store. This way I'll avoid
  many 'hopeless' characters that have to walk on level 6 still almost naked
  and have a choice between dying form hunger or dying killed by monsters.
- the 'no teleporting' law on the special levels (mainly the tower level)
  is a bit stupid - why not allow to teleport within the maze around the
  tower? Right now the easiest way to identify that you are on the tower level
  is to try to teleport.
- do something with those annoying 'friendly' mosters... In my game I had
  my last altar in a temple on level 12, so naturally I often came back to this
  level (in fact I had a kind of 'store' in the temple where I kept some
  items for later use). After some time the level was literaly filled with
  'friendly' elves, hobbits etc... Only I was not very friendly at this point,
  as every move was a pain (for me - to avoid them, and for my ATARI as
  well - to move them all). As a lawful one I kept myself from killing them,
  but I was really close to putting the helm of opposite alignment on ;-)
  (btw. HoOA was another item that had and ended ever using it). 
  Maybe if monsters can appear 'from nowhere' they could also 'disappear' 
  in the some way (with certain probability per monster - but only if they
  are friendly or they have not seen the character).

  OK, enough for a while, back to normal world. Believe or not, in so-called
real life I'm right now sitting on dungeon lvl 8 slowly running out of
food, with only a Swiss Army Knife for a weapon (great as a tin opener and 
lockpick as well) and in a +0 hard hat :-)
						Michal


